1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,073
The agent reaches the build server only through MCP tools. Every call goes to the audit log.

2
00:00:06,123 --> 00:00:12,381
Calls outside the agent's grant are refused: a check it may not run, an extra compiler flag.

3
00:00:12,431 --> 00:00:16,961
The release as it is fails the cross build: a target header is missing.

4
00:00:17,011 --> 00:00:23,005
The agent tries wrong repairs, like the unit tests' stub header. Each failed attempt counts.

5
00:00:23,055 --> 00:00:27,609
After the first attempt and three retries, the server refuses the next one.

6
00:00:27,659 --> 00:00:30,701
A person reads the audit log and resets the count.

7
00:00:30,751 --> 00:00:34,849
The right repair, the target sysroot, passes the build check.

8
00:00:34,899 --> 00:00:40,101
ThreadSanitizer in the unit check finds a data race that no analyser reported.

9
00:00:40,151 --> 00:00:45,113
With the race fixed, the plain, thread and address sanitizer runs pass.

10
00:00:45,163 --> 00:00:52,313
A fix with no test that names its finding fails the unit check.

11
00:00:52,363 --> 00:00:57,685
The release check fails and says why: unit failed, and there are no bench results yet.

12
00:00:57,735 --> 00:01:03,347
Every call behaved as expected. Waits are shortened; the real run took about 6 minutes.

